{"user": "Why wasn't I able to play A1 despite B1, B2 and A2 all being taken already", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T02:47:52.104164+00:00", "assistant": "Because in Othello, a square is legal **only if your move flips at least one White disc**.\n\nFor **a1**, Black would need a line like:\n\n- **a1\u2013b1\u2013c1...** = White(s) then a Black  \n- or **a1\u2013a2\u2013a3...** = White(s) then a Black  \n- or **a1\u2013b2\u2013c3...** = White(s) then a Black\n\nSo it\u2019s not enough that **b1, b2, and a2 are occupied**. They must be **White discs bracketed by a Black disc farther along the same line**.\n\nAlso, if **a1 was already occupied**, you can never play there at all.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T02:48:00.772620+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T02:48:02.699249+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 2}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
